  "body": "**P0 (#629):** every lathe thread was cut **left-hand**. The engine ran every pass toward +Z (away from the chuck), and the Fanuc Lathe post wrote `M03` and dropped the CL's arc sense. Confirmed against the control vendor's own behaviour: PathPilot Hub 8L conversational right-hand OD G76 runs toward −Z under M3. That sample is cited as behaviour confirmation only.\n\n## What changed\n- **Hand rule:** `cl::ThreadHand` (Right by default, or Left). A helix is RH if it turns ccw (seen from +Z) while rising, or cw while falling. With the free end at +Z, M03 means the tool goes cw around the part, so a cw half-turn needs M03 and a ccw one M04.\n- **Engine (`turning/thread.rs`):** every pass starts at the top and **descends toward the chuck**. Arc sense = `hand.ccw_for(true)`, and the infeed schedule is unchanged.\n- **Record and stream:**\n  - `ThreadCycle.hand`; `is_sane` requires every half-turn to wind that hand.\n  - The `THREAD … HAND right|left` word is required.\n  - `PARAM SpindleDirection \"reverse\"` is emitted when M04 is needed.\n  - New manifest flag `threadHands`: a script without it is refused a reverse section by name. Documented in CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md and assets/posts/AGENTS.md.\n- **fanuc-lathe.cps:**\n  - writes M03, or M04 (with an operator note) when the stream asks for reverse;\n  - checks **every G32 half-turn** against the spindle it wrote and refuses a mismatch (\"would cut the other hand\");\n  - G76 refuses a record with no hand, or one whose hand and Z direction need the other spindle.\n- **Verdict:** `thread_hand_warnings` raises a Gouge at the first wrong-hand half-turn, so the gate blocks.\n- **App:**\n  - `OpParams::Threading { hand }` (Right).\n  - The project file always writes `hand`; an old file loads as Right.\n  - The cache stamp includes the hand, so every old threading cache goes Stale once and regenerates toward the chuck.\n  - MCP picks it up through the params DTO.\n  - UI: a \"Hand\" row on the Passes tab, undoable.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/629-thread-hand.md` (no project version bump: reasoning inside; the feed-away-from-chuck option is left for a follow-up).\n\n**Golden diff** (`fanuc-lathe/thread_g76.nc`): `G00 X12.1 Z8` → `Z14`, and `G76 X9.6 Z14 …` → `Z8 …`. The cycle now starts at the top and feeds toward the chuck under M03.\n\n## How tested\n- **New tests (each fails on the old code):**\n  - motion: `every_pass_runs_toward_the_chuck_and_the_helix_winds_the_asked_hand` and `the_hand_of_a_turn_is_the_screw_law`;\n  - app `lathe_post_g76`: `a_right_hand_thread_posts_toward_the_chuck_under_m03` (18 G32 blocks descending, G76 Z14→Z8), `a_left_hand_thread_posts_toward_the_chuck_under_m04` and `the_hand_is_never_dropped`;\n  - `lathe_post_refusals`: ccw falling under M03 is refused;\n  - `turning_thread`: hand edit undo/redo;\n  - `project_roundtrip`: an old file loads as Right, Left survives, and an invalid word is refused;\n  - ui: the hand row.\n- **Gate:** motion, post, cl and the app lathe, turning, inverted, conformance, golden_cl, posting, project_roundtrip, commands_undo and mcp suites pass. Clippy is clean on 5 crates.\n\n## Follow-ups and merge notes\n- **#626 (PathPilot lathe post):** must declare `threadHands`, read `PARAM SpindleDirection`, check half-turn sense, and take the G76 direction from Z→EndZ.\n- **Threading stack (#516-#518, #468):** must carry `hand` and keep the descending passes and arc sense.\n\nChangelog: Lathe threads cut right-hand toward the chuck under M03 by default; Threading gains a Hand (Right/Left, LH posts M04), the thread record and stream state the hand, and the Fanuc Lathe post refuses any pass or G76 whose hand disagrees with its spindle (#629)\n\nFixes #629\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
